# GarmentLens — Core Rules

## Project Identity
- Internal garment repair intake tool: single store, ~200 garments/week
- Backend: Node.js 20 + Express 4 + SQLite + MinIO + OpenAI GPT-4o
- Frontend: React 18 + TypeScript 5 + Vite (no UI framework)
- DO NOT suggest technologies outside this stack without explicit approval

## Naming Conventions
- Variables and functions: `camelCase`
- React components, classes, types, interfaces: `PascalCase`
- Environment constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- Backend files: `camelCase.js` | React components: `PascalCase.tsx` | Hooks/utils: `camelCase.ts`

## Formatting
- 2-space indentation, no tabs
- Single quotes in JS/TS; double quotes in JSX attributes
- Trailing commas on all multiline objects and arrays
- Max line length: 120 characters
- No semicolons in plain JS files; semicolons required in TypeScript files

## Functions
- Arrow functions everywhere (callbacks, utilities, components)
- Named exports preferred over default exports
- Max 40 lines per function — extract helpers if longer
- One function, one responsibility

## Error Handling (non-negotiable)
- Always try/catch around async operations
- Backend always returns `{ error: "message" }` — never expose stack traces
- Frontend errors go into component state, never console.log in production paths
- Never silently swallow errors — log at minimum

## Comments
- No comments explaining WHAT — well-named identifiers do that
- Comments only for WHY: security decisions, non-obvious constraints, upstream bug workarounds
- Zero commented-out code in any commit

## Hard Constraints — Never Suggest These
- No authentication (single-user internal tool, deliberately excluded from MVP)
- No WebSockets (5s polling is correct at this volume)
- No Redis, Bull, or job queues (synchronous AI is MVP-appropriate)
- No Tailwind or any CSS framework (CSS variable system is the design system)
- No ORM — raw SQLite prepared statements only
- No frontend routing — single page app by design
